  "body": "## What changed\n\nSaved cut recipes hold an operation's parameters, its tool name, and its workpiece material. A user library stores them in `recipes.camrecipes`, with a `camcraft-recipes/1` envelope. The folder is `CAMCRAFT_RECIPES`, else `<platform data dir>/camcraft/recipes`.\n\n`ApplyCutRecipe` wraps `CreateOperation`. One undo removes the new operation. MCP tools `save_cut_recipe`, `list_cut_recipes`, and `apply_cut_recipe` use this library. Each tool accepts an optional `library` path. The generated MCP reference and the guide list the tools.\n\nThe caller supplies the new source. The command refuses a recipe by name if its saved parameters contain geometry that the API cannot replace. The audit covers:\n\n- Drill holes and cross holes; bore and thread holes.\n- Contour chain overrides and excluded deburr edges.\n- Contour start and exit picks.\n- Per-corner relief overrides of Pocket, Adaptive2D and Offset2D. A recipe with only the global relief kind still applies.\n- Tilted plane origins.\n- Circular centers, slot endpoints, probe targets, and undercut endpoints.\n- Wire start and sync points; sinker burn positions.\n- Waterjet tab positions. A waterjet recipe without tab positions still applies.\n\nThe command also refuses a missing tool, an unknown material, and a material mismatch. When a recipe names a material, the destination must have that material in force. An absent destination material now causes a refusal with the recipe name.\n\nThe library format stays the same. The decision record is `docs/decisions/3073-cut-recipes.md`.\n\n## Review fixes and pin proof\n\nThe first review found two defects. Applying a recipe copied geometry from its previous source. The material check also accepted an absent destination material.\n\nRegression pins in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe/safety.rs`:\n\n- `cut_recipe_does_not_transfer_holes_to_a_different_source`: transfer between plates with holes at different coordinates.\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_other_saved_coordinates_by_name`: other operations with saved coordinates.\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_saved_picks_and_plane_origins`: cross holes, entity picks, and tilted plane origins.\n- `cut_recipe_with_a_named_material_requires_a_destination_material`: command refusal when the destination material is absent.\n- `cut_recipe_mcp_refuses_an_absent_destination_material`: MCP refusal for the same case.\n\nThe second review found saved contour start and exit picks. The pins are in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe/picks.rs`.\n\nThe four original tests in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe.rs` also cover save, load, apply, generation, undo, and the existing refusals.\n\nMutation evidence: Removing the geometry guard made the geometry pins fail. Restoring the old material guard made both absent-material pins fail.\n\n### Review of `44191d272`: per-corner relief overrides\n\nThe review found that a saved per-corner relief override passed the audit. Each override holds a source corner XY. `has_saved_geometry` now checks `corner_relief.overrides` of Pocket, Adaptive2D and Offset2D.\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe/relief.rs`:\n\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_saved_corner_relief_overrides_by_name`: command refusal for the three kinds.\n- `cut_recipe_mcp_refuses_saved_corner_relief_overrides`: the MCP reproduction of the review (40 x 40 stock, override at `[20, 20]`, then 60 x 60 stock).\n- `cut_recipe_applies_global_corner_relief_without_overrides`: a global dogbone recipe applies for the three kinds.\n- `cut_recipe_mcp_applies_global_corner_relief`: a global dogbone recipe applies and generates through MCP.\n\nMutation evidence: with the new check removed, the two refusal pins failed (16 passed, 2 failed). With the check restored, all 18 recipe tests passed.\n\n### Review of `d8f36c3a2`: waterjet tab positions\n\nNewer `main` has `OpParams::WaterjetProfile` (#3058). The exhaustive `match` in `has_saved_geometry` did not cover it, so the trial merge did not compile. The branch now has a merge of `upstream/main` (`8473cb6a8`, no conflict) and the new arm (`e04a76c8e`). A tab position (`tabs.at`) is a world X, Y of the source contour. `ApplyCutRecipe` refuses a recipe whose `tabs.at` is not empty. A waterjet recipe without tab positions applies.\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/cut_recipe/waterjet.rs`:\n\n- `cut_recipe_refuses_saved_waterjet_tab_positions_by_name`: command refusal. The same parameters are legal in `CreateOperation`.\n- `cut_recipe_applies_a_waterjet_recipe_without_tab_positions`: the recipe applies and generates.\n\nMutation evidence: with the arm changed to `false`, the refusal pin failed (19 passed, 1 failed). With the arm restored, all 20 recipe tests passed.\n\n## Final validation\n\nHead: `e04a76c8e979db89db4bf73e3e55c304ffc1f220`\nBase: `upstream/main` at `ddc4d82741f65f483cdadcddb256464fb56ab883`. The head contains a merge of that base. All gates ran on the merged head.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 364 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (22.5 minutes).\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 219 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (29.8 minutes).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n- `app suites: cut_recipe`: 20 passed, 0 failed.\n- `app suites: example_catalog` and `app suites: first_router_part` passed in the quick gate. `app heavy: example_catalog` passed in the heavy gate.\n- The golden suites that the diff reaches ran in the quick gate. All passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light` did not run in this round.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. After the catalog suite and the gates ran, the working tree was clean. No recorded program or golden file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- UI screenshots do not apply. This PR changes no UI files.\n- There is no GUI recipe panel. Issue #3393 holds that work.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill has no row for the new tools. This PR supplies the generated reference and guide entries.\n- Recipes omit coolant and area controls. Coolant depends on the machine. Area controls depend on the geometry.\n- Automatic geometry matching is not exercised. The command refuses recipes that need replacement geometry.\n- Replacement coordinates for relief overrides are not supplied. The command refuses such a recipe.\n- The knowledge graph could not be updated because `graphify` is not installed on this host.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Saved cut recipes: save an operation's settings under a name and apply them to new geometry in one undoable step (MCP `save_cut_recipe`, `list_cut_recipes`, `apply_cut_recipe`); a recipe whose tool or material is gone is refused by name.\n\nFixes #3073\n\n",
